## Candidate Schema

The canonical TSV header is:

```text
candidate_id target_world claim provider resources information falsification divergence token_cost wall_cost gpu_cost quota_cost risk evidence_sha256 falsifier_sha256
```

The real separator is a tab. `resources` is a comma-separated, sorted, unique,
nonempty set of exact identities. The compiler accepts 1 through 18 candidates.
Token and wall costs are positive; GPU and quota costs may be zero. Every score
axis is in `1..1000` and candidate risk is in `0..1000`.

## Exact Frontier

A feasible portfolio is nonempty, fits all four budgets, and contains no
repeated exact resource. Portfolio A Pareto-dominates B only if A is no worse in
all three benefit axes, risk, and all four costs, and is strictly better in at
least one. The compiler retains every non-dominated portfolio.

V0 materializes at most 256 skyline members and 1 MiB of canonical frontier.
Crossing either limit refuses before an event or resource reservation. Thus
every accepted result is exact; pathological exponential fronts are reported
as unsupported rather than truncated or approximated.

One explicit policy then selects from that frontier:

```text
information-first    = information, falsification, divergence, lower risk, lower token, wall, GPU, quota
falsification-first  = falsification, information, divergence, lower risk, lower token, wall, GPU, quota
counterfactual-first = divergence, falsification, information, lower risk, lower token, wall, GPU, quota
```

The sorted selected candidate IDs are the final stable tie-break. The canonical
candidate set, canonical frontier, selected set, and their digests are retained
inside the hash-chained event. Replay enumerates the frontier again rather than
trusting those stored projections.

The compile event is also the atomic multi-resource reservation. Completion
releases the entire selected union with one outcome digest and the same owner
and generation.

## Falsification Conditions

- exact enumeration omits a feasible subset or retains a dominated subset;
- an oversized frontier is truncated, approximated, or partially committed
  instead of refusing fail-closed;
- the stored frontier or selected portfolio differs from replay;
- a selected portfolio exceeds any budget or repeats a resource;
- any frontier rival precedes the selected portfolio under its declared policy;
- removing only `portfolio_selected_not_dominated` does not admit the exact
  otherwise-refused dominated comparison frame;
- any selected target world or claim is absent;
- any resource is simultaneously live in a capability, single attention plan,
  or another portfolio;
- completion changes owner/generation or omits an outcome digest;
- a mutated portfolio event contributes an Arrow row;
- a model, UI, Arrow table, or provider CLI becomes scheduling authority.
